1
00:00:21,673 --> 00:00:23,193
The End No way we got it!

2
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:26,250
That treasure's been at the bottom
of the ocean for a hundred years!

3
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:27,970
And now whatever's in it is ours!

4
00:00:28,053 --> 00:00:29,213
Hey, stay calm.

5
00:00:29,473 --> 00:00:31,710
We gotta get it on the boat
before we start celebrating.

6
00:00:31,793 --> 00:00:33,093
Yeah, I know, I know.

7
00:00:33,313 --> 00:00:34,273
Up we go!

8
00:00:34,693 --> 00:00:37,690
That thing looks too long and
narrow to be a treasure chest.

9
00:00:37,773 --> 00:00:38,773
Just do your job!

10
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:40,501
You're lifting it too high!

11
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:42,553
Okay, on three.

12
00:00:43,413 --> 00:00:45,193
One, two, three!

13
00:00:46,073 --> 00:00:46,953
All right.

14
00:00:47,353 --> 00:00:48,750
Come on, crack it open, O 'Rish.

15
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:49,663
Hold on, wait.

16
00:00:49,773 --> 00:00:50,714
This is bizarre.

17
00:00:51,193 --> 00:00:53,970
It seems like this thing
was locked from the inside.

18
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:54,990
Who the hell cares?

19
00:00:55,073 --> 00:00:55,990
Just bust it open!

20
00:00:56,073 --> 00:00:57,253
Just give me a sec.

21
00:00:57,533 --> 00:00:59,062
Something's written on it.

22
00:01:00,073 --> 00:01:02,753
D-I-O. D-O?

23
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:03,770
Is that someone's name?

24
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:04,773
I don't care!

25
00:01:05,153 --> 00:01:06,653
Just freaking open it up!

26
00:01:06,953 --> 00:01:10,650
The sun's about to go down and I don't
want to be counting treasure in the dark!

27
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:12,713
Okay, I hear ya. Hmm.

28
00:01:13,053 --> 00:01:14,750
I'm gonna go get the blowtorch.

29
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:17,362
And then we can start
dividing up our loot!

30
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:24,630
On a day like any other, a motorboat
was found adrift and abandoned.

31
00:01:24,713 --> 00:01:28,973
The craft was largely undamaged
and showed no signs of struggle.

32
00:01:30,953 --> 00:01:31,783
In the galley,

33
00:01:32,053 --> 00:01:34,253
three cups of coffee sat half-full,

34
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:38,513
and on deck, an iron chest,
its lock melted away,

35
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,713
lay open and empty.

36
00:01:41,453 --> 00:01:47,113
But the chest's unusual shelter-like
chambers baffled discoverers,

37
00:01:47,213 --> 00:01:50,733
who believed it to have once
contained a vast treasure.

38
00:01:51,293 --> 00:01:56,433
But interest waned, and before
long, the chest was forgotten.

39
00:02:01,553 --> 00:02:07,433
Jotaro Kujo, 17 years old
and 195 centimeters tall.

40
00:02:07,993 --> 00:02:11,693
His father is a Japanese jazz
musician, currently on tour.

41
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:15,633
His mother is an American
of British descent.

42
00:02:16,033 --> 00:02:19,730
Yes, all of that is correct,
and Jotaro is definitely my son.

43
00:02:19,813 --> 00:02:22,010
It seems like all his
friends call him Jojo.

44
00:02:22,093 --> 00:02:23,950
Guess they decided to take
the Joe from his first

45
00:02:24,033 --> 00:02:26,650
name and the Joe from his
last name and combine them.

46
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:28,493
Oh man, that's really lame.

47
00:02:29,833 --> 00:02:31,370
I need to know.

48
00:02:31,453 --> 00:02:33,806
Exactly how many people did Jotaro kill?

49
00:02:33,913 --> 00:02:35,173
No, I take it back.

50
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:36,163
I don't want to know.

51
00:02:36,246 --> 00:02:37,076
Settle down.

52
00:02:37,159 --> 00:02:38,670
Nobody said anything
about him killing people.

53
00:02:38,753 --> 00:02:40,390
He got into a fight, that's all.

54
00:02:40,473 --> 00:02:44,650
The truth is, the thugs he tangled with
were all armed with nunchucks and knives.

55
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:49,150
He fought four punks, one being an
ex-boxer, and he broke 15 of their bones.

56
00:02:49,233 --> 00:02:51,073
And he busted their balls.

57
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:52,710
Sorry if that was crude.

58
00:02:52,793 --> 00:02:54,490
He put all of them in a hospital.

59
00:02:54,573 --> 00:02:55,890
Things could have gone a lot worse.

60
00:02:55,973 --> 00:02:58,070
He's got to be shown the
severity of his actions.

61
00:02:58,153 --> 00:02:58,983
Okay.

62
00:02:59,313 --> 00:03:01,784
The real issue is what happened afterward.

63
00:03:01,893 --> 00:03:03,050
Copy this and pass it around.

64
00:03:03,133 --> 00:03:03,963
Yes, sir.

65
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:06,930
I got to tell you, that son
of yours is a strange one.

66
00:03:07,013 --> 00:03:07,843
Huh?

67
00:03:09,533 --> 00:03:10,593
Okay, follow me.

68
00:03:10,733 --> 00:03:11,710
I'll show you the way.

69
00:03:11,793 --> 00:03:12,990
Thank you for everything.

70
00:03:13,073 --> 00:03:15,410
Look, you can thank me
by taking your kid home.

71
00:03:15,493 --> 00:03:17,590
So then, does that mean
you're releasing him?

72
00:03:17,673 --> 00:03:20,026
Well, we can't keep him in here forever.

73
00:03:20,393 --> 00:03:21,223
Okay.

74
00:03:21,306 --> 00:03:24,790
By the way, ma 'am, I have to tell you,
your Japanese is really quite good.

75
00:03:24,873 --> 00:03:27,010
Just how long have you
been living in Japan?

76
00:03:27,093 --> 00:03:28,353
For 20 years now.

77
00:03:28,593 --> 00:03:30,130
Well, that explains it then.

78
00:03:30,213 --> 00:03:31,095
Good work, man.

79
00:03:31,273 --> 00:03:33,373
This place has been overrun lately.

80
00:03:33,533 --> 00:03:37,610
We've got an entire backlog of criminals
that we aren't even able to find cells for.

81
00:03:37,693 --> 00:03:38,650
We're almost there, ma 'am.

82
00:03:38,733 --> 00:03:40,204
Your son's just up ahead.

83
00:03:40,793 --> 00:03:41,623
Jotaro!

84
00:03:44,013 --> 00:03:44,843
Jotaro!

85
00:03:44,926 --> 00:03:46,107
Throw the ball to mom!

86
00:03:47,673 --> 00:03:48,953
That's it. Good boy.

87
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:52,973
Do your best at that track
meet tomorrow. I will.

88
00:03:54,473 --> 00:03:56,013
Jotaro, you did it.

89
00:03:56,173 --> 00:03:58,110
Let's go out to eat and celebrate.

90
00:03:58,193 --> 00:04:00,487
Nothing's as good as your cooking, Mom.

91
00:04:01,653 --> 00:04:07,553
Jotaro, Jotaro, Jotaro, Jotaro, Jotaro!

92
00:04:08,973 --> 00:04:10,073
Shut up!

93
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:12,553
Get out of my face, you bitch!

94
00:04:23,273 --> 00:04:26,370
I promise you he's a
very sweet boy he's just

95
00:04:26,453 --> 00:04:28,350
not capable of doing
something so appalling.

96
00:04:28,433 --> 00:04:31,810
Hey on your feet Kujo
you're being released

97
00:04:31,893 --> 00:04:34,364
what part of go home don't you understand?

98
00:04:42,653 --> 00:04:44,453
Listen, Mom, you can leave.

99
00:04:44,933 --> 00:04:46,913
I'll be staying here for a while.

100
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:50,490
Seems I've been possessed
by an evil spirit,

101
00:04:50,573 --> 00:04:53,133
and I've no idea what'll make me do next.

102
00:04:53,773 --> 00:04:57,153
During that fight, it took
all I had just to stop it.

103
00:04:57,673 --> 00:05:00,555
So do everyone a favor
and leave me in this cage.

104
00:05:01,953 --> 00:05:05,150
Jeez, for crying out loud, do
you see what I'm talking about?

105
00:05:05,233 --> 00:05:07,690
We're trying to release
him, but he refuses to go.

106
00:05:07,773 --> 00:05:10,213
I'm sorry to have to ask you this,

107
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:13,090
but are you sure everything's
all right with your boy upstairs?

108
00:05:13,173 --> 00:05:15,349
This isn't a hotel, you know, ma 'am.

109
00:05:15,653 --> 00:05:17,829
Come on, let us change cells, please!

110
00:05:18,093 --> 00:05:20,387
Stop lying about the evil spirit thing!

111
00:05:22,833 --> 00:05:24,710
All right, all right, that's enough!

112
00:05:24,793 --> 00:05:25,734
Oh, you shut up!

113
00:05:34,073 --> 00:05:34,903
Is he?

114
00:05:34,986 --> 00:05:35,816
Seriously?

115
00:05:35,899 --> 00:05:37,430
What are you doing with
a beer in a jail cell?

116
00:05:37,513 --> 00:05:39,572
How did you even get that in there?

117
00:05:42,113 --> 00:05:43,153
I told you.

118
00:05:43,513 --> 00:05:44,973
I've got an evil spirit.

119
00:05:45,593 --> 00:05:48,064
And sometimes it likes to bring me things.

120
00:05:48,713 --> 00:05:49,833
What the hell?

121
00:05:50,193 --> 00:05:53,252
He's written Shonen Jump
while listening to a radio.

122
00:05:53,593 --> 00:05:55,470
Sir, I mean, how is this even possible?

123
00:05:55,553 --> 00:05:56,990
We have a major problem here.

124
00:05:57,073 --> 00:05:57,903
Hold it.

125
00:05:59,153 --> 00:06:02,630
This might not be enough to make
you guys keep me locked up in here.

126
00:06:02,713 --> 00:06:05,537
But I'll show you how
evil the spirit is anyway.

127
00:06:05,873 --> 00:06:09,713
Maybe then you'll see why letting
me out of here is a bad idea.

128
00:06:23,233 --> 00:06:24,990
That's my gun he has in his hand!

129
00:06:25,073 --> 00:06:25,903
But howdy!

130
00:06:25,986 --> 00:06:26,816
That's really bad!

131
00:06:26,973 --> 00:06:28,593
You didn't see it just now?

132
00:06:28,773 --> 00:06:32,733
Well, if you guys didn't see my
evil spirit, then watch this.

133
00:06:35,413 --> 00:06:36,933
No! Jotaro!

134
00:06:48,753 --> 00:06:53,833
It's like there's someone behind me
that bound itself to me not long ago.

135
00:06:56,393 --> 00:06:59,373
Jotaro's grandfather
Joseph has strange powers.

136
00:07:01,173 --> 00:07:02,997
But what's happening to my son?

137
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,223
Papa!

138
00:07:16,493 --> 00:07:17,323
Hmm?

139
00:07:17,406 --> 00:07:18,653
Over here, Papa! Over here!

140
00:07:19,493 --> 00:07:20,323
Holly!

141
00:07:20,406 --> 00:07:21,236
Out of my way!

142
00:07:21,319 --> 00:07:22,575
Oh, I can't believe you're here!

143
00:07:24,513 --> 00:07:25,793
Thank you for coming.

144
00:07:26,053 --> 00:07:27,790
Hey, you're my one and only daughter,

145
00:07:27,873 --> 00:07:29,950
and if you tell me you
need me to be somewhere?

146
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:32,915
then just give me a day
and I'll cross the globe.

147
00:07:33,633 --> 00:07:34,570
Did Mom come?

148
00:07:34,653 --> 00:07:36,170
She didn't like me leaving,

149
00:07:36,253 --> 00:07:39,990
but I just told Susie that it was
official Joestar Corporation business,

150
00:07:40,073 --> 00:07:41,133
and I had to go.

151
00:07:42,693 --> 00:07:43,873
Thanks, Papa.

152
00:07:45,153 --> 00:07:45,983
Holly.

153
00:07:47,433 --> 00:07:50,270
Hey, the greetings over
let go of me already.

154
00:07:50,353 --> 00:07:55,593
No, I don't wanna it's been forever
since you've held me look at yourself.

155
00:07:56,153 --> 00:07:56,983
Come on.

156
00:07:57,113 --> 00:07:59,633
You're a 45 year old woman. Let go.

157
00:07:59,773 --> 00:08:01,170
Oh now you've done it.

158
00:08:01,253 --> 00:08:02,083
I'm gonna

159
00:08:08,233 --> 00:08:10,473
Hey, what are you clowns staring at?

160
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:12,063
Don't look.

161
00:08:12,146 --> 00:08:13,131
I'll take your bag.

162
00:08:13,233 --> 00:08:15,273
By the way, Holly, about Jotaro.

163
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:18,593
You sure he used the word evil spirit?

164
00:08:21,153 --> 00:08:22,953
Oh, my poor little boy.

165
00:08:23,313 --> 00:08:26,813
Yes, the policeman said they
couldn't see it, but I saw it.

166
00:08:26,973 --> 00:08:28,679
It's like he had a third arm.

167
00:08:29,113 --> 00:08:31,630
And then he reached out
and grabbed the gun.

168
00:08:31,713 --> 00:08:35,470
And when this arm came out, no one
else there could see it but you?

169
00:08:35,553 --> 00:08:36,383
That's right.

170
00:08:36,773 --> 00:08:40,090
And aside from Jotaro saying that
he's been possessed, you're okay?

171
00:08:40,173 --> 00:08:41,550
Did anything happen to you?

172
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:42,953
I feel totally fine.

173
00:08:43,093 --> 00:08:44,858
But what do I do about Jotaro?

174
00:08:45,053 --> 00:08:48,070
He says he won't leave that cell
until he finds the cause of all this.

175
00:08:48,153 --> 00:08:49,390
What am I going to do, Papa?

176
00:08:49,473 --> 00:08:51,470
There, there, my darling daughter.

177
00:08:51,553 --> 00:08:53,847
You've got Joseph Joestar with you now.

178
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:55,793
No need to worry. Thank you.

179
00:09:00,553 --> 00:09:02,393
Now let's go see my grandson.

180
00:09:03,693 --> 00:09:05,575
Jotaro can explain this himself.

181
00:09:16,633 --> 00:09:18,153
It's getting spookier.

182
00:09:18,353 --> 00:09:20,350
He's got more stuff in his cell now.

183
00:09:20,433 --> 00:09:21,553
And he's violent.

184
00:09:21,913 --> 00:09:24,850
If something is possessing him,
it's definitely not something nice.

185
00:09:24,933 --> 00:09:30,013
If word of this gets out to my superiors,
I'll lose my job in a heartbeat for sure!

186
00:09:30,493 --> 00:09:32,140
He's no longer your problem.

187
00:09:32,433 --> 00:09:34,551
I'll be taking my grandson home now.

188
00:09:34,773 --> 00:09:35,603
Your grandson?

189
00:09:36,153 --> 00:09:36,983
Hold it!

190
00:09:37,066 --> 00:09:37,896
That's far enough!

191
00:09:37,979 --> 00:09:39,270
You're better off just
staying where you are!

192
00:09:39,353 --> 00:09:40,235
It's dangerous!

193
00:09:40,593 --> 00:09:42,030
Convince him to leave him
where you're standing!

194
00:09:42,113 --> 00:09:43,130
I'll take my chances!

195
00:09:43,213 --> 00:09:44,650
Now step aside and leave him to me!

196
00:09:44,733 --> 00:09:46,439
We won't be held as possible!

197
00:09:47,453 --> 00:09:48,283
Move it!

198
00:09:48,366 --> 00:09:49,196
Jotaro!

199
00:09:49,279 --> 00:09:50,444
This is your grandfather!

200
00:09:50,873 --> 00:09:53,350
Whatever's happened,
he'll be able to help you!

201
00:09:53,433 --> 00:09:55,315
Please come out and talk to him!

202
00:10:03,513 --> 00:10:04,433
Come out.

203
00:10:04,673 --> 00:10:05,933
It's time to go home.

204
00:10:06,873 --> 00:10:08,073
Get lost.

205
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:10,098
I didn't ask you to come here.

206
00:10:10,413 --> 00:10:12,354
You really think you can help me?

207
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:14,633
An old man like yourself?

208
00:10:15,253 --> 00:10:20,233
Sorry you came all the way from New
York, but nobody can help me, Gramps.

209
00:10:21,413 --> 00:10:22,243
Huh?

210
00:10:23,613 --> 00:10:26,670
Wait that's the pinky from
my prosthetic left hand

211
00:10:26,753 --> 00:10:31,410
when was he able to take
it so Did you see it or

212
00:10:31,493 --> 00:10:36,410
even feel it that's the
evil spirit stay away from

213
00:10:36,493 --> 00:10:41,130
me or you'll Lose what's
left of your life I've

214
00:10:41,213 --> 00:10:44,310
never seen anything like
this he was able to Deceive

215
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:47,830
me right off the bat that's
unbelievable I'm afraid

216
00:10:47,913 --> 00:10:51,270
I know exactly What Jotaro's
evil spirit is but I

217
00:10:51,353 --> 00:10:53,690
don't think explaining it
to him will do any good.

218
00:10:53,773 --> 00:10:58,170
He'll understand his situation much
better if he sees it with his own eyes.

219
00:10:58,253 --> 00:11:01,630
Actually, in order for him to
truly know the danger he faces,

220
00:11:01,713 --> 00:11:04,053
he needs to experience it physically.

221
00:11:05,673 --> 00:11:08,513
All right, Avdol, it's your turn now.

222
00:11:09,573 --> 00:11:13,220
I'd like you to meet an Egyptian
friend I met a few years ago.

223
00:11:13,633 --> 00:11:15,673
Say hello to Avdol.

224
00:11:17,553 --> 00:11:20,530
Do what you need to just
get my grandson to leave

225
00:11:20,613 --> 00:11:24,150
this damn cell back off
you look strong enough.

226
00:11:24,233 --> 00:11:27,030
But do you really think
I'd let someone chase me

227
00:11:27,113 --> 00:11:29,937
out of here just because
you told them to do it?

228
00:11:30,173 --> 00:11:33,650
I don't work like that
in fact all you've done

229
00:11:33,733 --> 00:11:36,190
now is made me want to
stay here even more.

230
00:11:36,273 --> 00:11:39,690
I'm afraid this may get
a little bit rough but in

231
00:11:39,773 --> 00:11:42,170
a few minutes he'll be
riddled with so much pain.

232
00:11:42,253 --> 00:11:44,810
But he'll be begging you
to let him out of here.

233
00:11:44,893 --> 00:11:46,010
Just do what you gotta do.

234
00:11:46,093 --> 00:11:46,923
Papa!

235
00:11:47,006 --> 00:11:48,673
You can't be serious! Wait a sec!

236
00:11:48,953 --> 00:11:49,870
We can't let you turn this!

237
00:11:49,953 --> 00:11:51,313
Sip it, pig! Yes, sir!

238
00:12:09,153 --> 00:12:09,983
This is...

239
00:12:10,853 --> 00:12:11,683
That's right.

240
00:12:12,313 --> 00:12:15,019
Avdol also has what you'd
call an evil spirit.

241
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:18,713
An evil spirit under the
complete command of Avdol's will.

242
00:12:18,853 --> 00:12:19,912
And his name is...

243
00:12:21,053 --> 00:12:22,073
Magician's Red!

244
00:12:27,713 --> 00:12:28,553
It's hot.

245
00:12:28,833 --> 00:12:30,373
I feel like I'm on fire.

246
00:12:30,813 --> 00:12:32,573
My arms, they're burning.

247
00:12:33,133 --> 00:12:35,013
What are these evil spirits?

248
00:12:35,313 --> 00:12:36,433
What's Cujoh doing?

249
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:38,710
Why's he flattening himself
against the back wall?

250
00:12:38,793 --> 00:12:39,890
Yeah, I don't get it.

251
00:12:39,973 --> 00:12:42,430
But do you feel how hot
